      "writtenOn": "2020-03-20T01:53:04Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I stands for internal here. So, I think this is fine.\n\nOn mt_scp, we save both intruction and data on SRAM (i.e. IRAM) at first.\nBy the need of protecting the SCP firmware, we separate the instruction, rodata and data to IROM and IRAM respectively. And, we then use MPU to protect the IROM region. That\u0027s how the name comes from.",
      "parentUuid": "7d70b20b_53380334",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 219,
        "startChar": 5,
        "endLine": 219,
        "endChar": 9
      },
